Hi everyone. I'm back on again after a brief hiatus.
I've got a version of Nethack3.0f for the Mac ready for
testing.  It's approximately 500K. I've already tested
it on a Mac II, IIcx, SE and Plus w/HDs. It needs 700K of memory
so remove your fonts and DAs if you've got a one meg machine.
Email me if you'd like a copy. (Sorry for those people who
mailed me their address while I was at Waterloo,  but
I misplaced the sheet with everyone's address during my move).

Features of MacNetHack3:
If it can't find a file it'll ask you.
Icons for nethack-created files.
You can double-click on a save file and nethack will run.
You can store your save file anywhere.
Colour support for those lucky and/or rich enough.
Faster text output. (Still noticeably slow on a Plus but
  almost like an arcade game on a II).
Smaller save files on average i.e. 6-10K usual size.
  IBM PC character set for dungeon (appropriated from
  ZTERM (if anyone knows the authour's address please send
  it along, I'd like to get his permission to use the font))
 
I'll be applying the level 3 patches this weekend and hopefully
, if my eyes don't fail me, I'll have a new version by Monday -
maybe sooner.

I have had the program crash on me at random intervals so be wary.
I'm still using Raid on the program.

